3. UNDERLYING MATERIAL — HMMT
===============================================================================

The HMMT February 2026 problem set is competition material of the Harvard-MIT
Mathematics Tournament (HMMT), a student-run tournament organised by students
of Harvard University and the Massachusetts Institute of Technology
(February 14, 2026 sitting). The mirror above republishes the problems for LLM
evaluation. This pack redistributes them solely for non-commercial
benchmarking and research, with attribution to the upstream mirror and to HMMT
as the origin of the contest. Nothing here implies HMMT endorsement.

===============================================================================
4. VENDORED FILE — data/hmmt_feb_2026.jsonl
===============================================================================

33 records, one per line:
  {"problem_idx": 1..33, "problem": "<verbatim statement>",
   "answer": "<verbatim final answer>", "problem_type": ["<label>", ...]}
SHA-256: fbcd8e4f4325f98ec90c9064119c3f4f8b423de81b548643f43e0d725e5a71d4

The file is a faithful projection of the upstream parquet: `problem` and
`answer` verbatim; `problem_type` values with surrounding whitespace stripped
(the upstream list values carry a leading space on all but the first entry).
The file is pinned in scripts/generate-dataset.mjs; the pack build fails if it
changes. scripts/derive-dataset.py regenerates it from the pinned parquet.
